# This directory holds blog AUTHORING SOURCE (markdown drafts and source
# images), not web content. Nothing on the site links to it.
#
# It must not be web-readable: it contains drafts for posts that have not
# been published yet (Blog-4, Blog-5, Blog-6), and serving the .md source of
# a published post alongside the real page would be duplicate content.
#
# The deny is matched on an extension, so it covers every file in here while
# leaving the extensionless directory name itself alone. Denying the
# directory would also reject the /blog URL, because access control resolves
# from the directory mapping before mod_rewrite routes /blog to
# blog-full-list.php.
<FilesMatch "\.[A-Za-z0-9]+$">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# The /blog URL is the blog index, routed to blog-full-list.php by the root
# .htaccess. Without this, mod_dir would first 301 /blog to /blog/ because
# this directory exists, and that redirect would shadow the route. Scoped
# here rather than site-wide so other directories (/Admin, /css, /images)
# keep their normal trailing-slash redirect.
DirectorySlash Off
